differential2 §11b residual: non-data-descriptor (method) shadowing.
PLR: an instance attribute shadows a same-named method, so after
c.m = 99, c.m == 99. CBMC models methods on the method-call path, not
as shadowable instance-dict entries, so the instance assignment does
not override the method read. The KNOWNBUG regex states the
PLR-correct outcome; faithful modeling needs instance-dict-as-storage.
